<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mostly higher.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mostly higher.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark Northern Spring wheat cash bids were mostly higher, underpinned by slow farm sales, dealers said.</p>
<p>A Minneapolis dealer noted some movement of 15 percent high protein spring wheat out of the Dakotas and Minnesota.</p>
<p>Dealers expressed concerns about the lack of exports.</p>
<p>&quot;We need some export business and I don't see that happening anytime soon,&quot; one said.</p>
<p>&quot;Everybody is waiting for wheat prices to improve,&quot; a Montana broker said.</p>
<p>Domestic mills were also buying some nearby wheat, a second Montana dealer said.</p>
<p>MGE December wheat ended at $4.10-1/4 a bushel, up 3/4 cent, while the rest of the board was 1/2 to eight cents lower.  </p>
